{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
JSON-LD shippingDetails for one Offer (no surrounding braces: render inside an Offer object)

* product: the product
* price: the offer's price in pence (variant.price); defaults to product.price

UK delivery (owner, 13 Oct 2026): free over £25, otherwise £3.50. Country code is ISO 3166-1 ("GB", not "UK").
Gift cards ship nothing, so they get no shippingDetails: callers check product.gift_card? before rendering.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign offer_price = price | default: product.price
  comment
    Must match the Shopify "Domestic" shipping rates (Settings > Shipping). On 13 Oct 2026 Shopify gave free delivery
    from £24.00 while the site copy says over £25: keep this number equal to Shopify's.
  endcomment
  assign free_delivery_from = 2500
  assign shipping_rate = 3.5
  if offer_price >= free_delivery_from
    assign shipping_rate = 0
  endif
-%}
"shippingDetails": {
  "@type": "OfferShippingDetails",
  "shippingRate": {
    "@type": "MonetaryAmount",
    "value": {{ shipping_rate | json }},
    "currency": "GBP"
  },
  "shippingDestination": {
    "@type": "DefinedRegion",
    "addressCountry": "GB"
  },
  "deliveryTime": {
    "@type": "ShippingDeliveryTime",
    "handlingTime": {
      "@type": "QuantitativeValue",
      "minValue": 0,
      "maxValue": 1,
      "unitCode": "DAY"
    },
    "transitTime": {
      "@type": "QuantitativeValue",
      "minValue": 1,
      "maxValue": 2,
      "unitCode": "DAY"
    }
  }
}
